The heat energy generated when a 1000-gram metal block falls 10 meters can be calculated by considering the gravitational potential energy lost, as all energy goes into heat. The mass is 1 kg, gravitational acceleration is 9.8 m/s², and height is 10 m. The potential energy is:

\[
\text{GPE} = m \cdot g \cdot h = 1 \cdot 9.8 \cdot 10 = 98 \, \text{joules}.
\]

Converting joules to calories (1 calorie ≈ 4.184 joules):

\[
98 \, \text{joules} \div 4.184 \, \text{joules/calorie} \approx 23.5 \, \text{calories}.
\]

Thus, the heat energy is approximately 23.5 calories, corresponding to option F.

Answer: F. 23.5 cal
